    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d407">

                <pb facs="0510" n="500" xml:id="pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.67/3–1347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-13T20:00:00-05:00">March 13, 1947—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>510. Provided Secretary Marshall perceives no objection please reply (urtel 643
                    Mar. 4, 8 p.m.) Mar 3 FonOff note in sense of Deptel 199 Feb 7, 7 p.m.<anchor
                        n="44" xml:id="d407-f1"/> to effect that we plan utilize commercial vessel
                    for diplomatic couriers proceeding Dairen as soon as such vessels are available;
                    however as Soviet Consul Dairen has stated to US ConGen there (Dairen’s 13 Jan
                    18) that port presently is closed to trade. In view obvious impracticability
                    diverting commercial steamers long distances involved merely afford passage to
                    couriers and constant availability only overnight trip away small naval vessel
                    specially disarmed for this purpose we consider only practicable interim
                    solution is to continue to use that (Sent Moscow repeated Nanking) vessel.</p>
                <p>For Emb’s info prior to Mr. Cohen’s<anchor n="45" xml:id="d407-f2"/> departure he
                    was given file on Dairen courier service.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d407-f1" n="44" xml:id="d407-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 27, <ref target="#pg493">p. 493</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d407-f2" n="45" xml:id="d407-f2-content">
                <p>Benjamin V. Cohen, Counselor of the Department, member of the American delegation
                    to the Council of Foreign Ministers at Moscow.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
